All 28 confirmed problems are fixed, except one I'm deliberately leaving: the few seconds the keystroke check adds per field. All 102 tests pass, and fair-play is clean (it caught one public number I had copied into a comment). The calculation gives the same answer as before on all 25 real inputs from our runs; the changes only matter for formats the public data never had.

**What's now fixed, in plain terms:**
- **The two serious ones:**
  - A second TAN reader is no longer sent away from the right message.
  - A status legend containing "gesperrt" no longer counts as a blocked material.
- **Number and date reading:**
  - a number annotated "German format" read 100× too large;
  - days and weeks mixed up when both appear;
  - an exchange-rate note misread, and a false "missing exchange rate";
  - a quantity change later on the scenario day wrongly applied.
- **Clicks, the TAN and logins:**
  - a false "the form was not sent" on script-driven buttons;
  - a 3-second wait on buttons that are already gone;
  - the TAN looked for on the wrong site when the plan is vague;
  - a browser TAN pop-up answered with an old TAN;
  - no login on the fresh-tab fallback.
- **Robustness:**
  - the submitter gave up after 4 slow model answers; it now keeps trying until its deadline;
  - helpers stuck on unusual identifier shapes;
  - agents chasing outdated gap lists;
  - gap agents not stopped at the cutoff;
  - gap checks waiting too long on sites without a mailbox.

**Where things stand:**
- **The final currently uses run #16's code** (`sub_e66e`, submitted from the website), which still has the two serious problems. Once the fixed version scores 100 on a public run, it should replace it.
- **Best of 3 is still off.** You need to run `~/.local/bin/atira final --best-of 3` yourself.

Shall I start run #17 with the fixed code? It's one test run, about 11 minutes and $0.40, and it doesn't touch your submission.

